From: wayland nvidia crash investigation
Subject: [PATCH] gdk/wayland: do not attach an SHM buffer to an EGL-backed surface

gdk_cairo_draw_from_gl() creates the window's paint GL context, and with it the EGL surface for the toplevel wl_surface, from inside a draw handler. When the frame in progress began as a cairo/SHM frame, current_paint.use_gl is FALSE for
that frame, so end_paint attaches the SHM buffer to a surface that the EGL implementation has meanwhile taken over.

On Nvidia, egl-wayland arms explicit sync (wp_linux_drm_syncobj_surface_v1) for every EGLSurface, so that attach has no acquire point and the compositor raises a protocol error: "explicit sync is used, but no acquire point is set", which
GDK reports as "Error 71 (Protocol error) dispatching to Wayland display".

Skip the attach once the window is EGL-backed. The next frame is a GL frame and paints the correct contents.

See https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/issues/8056
---
 gdk/wayland/gdkwindow-wayland.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/gdk/wayland/gdkwindow-wayland.c
+++ b/gdk/wayland/gdkwindow-wayland.c
@@ -905,6 +905,12 @@ gdk_wayland_window_attach_image (GdkWindow *window)
   if (GDK_WINDOW_DESTROYED (window))
     return;
 
+  /* The EGL implementation owns the buffer state of this surface once an EGL
+   * window has been created for it, and may have armed explicit sync on it.
+   * Attaching an SHM buffer here is a protocol error in that case. */
+  if (impl->display_server.egl_window != NULL || impl->egl_surface != NULL)
+    return;
+
   g_assert (_gdk_wayland_is_shm_surface (impl->staging_cairo_surface));
 
   /* Attach this new buffer to the surface */
